speechtext:
If the minister will recall, he gave the extra ones to Nova Scotia, Saskatchewan and British Columbia, so that Manitoba remains at sixteen, whereas they had seventeen. That is as I followed the minister;
I may be wrong.
Mr. ST. LAURENT: I am sorry, but I handed the statement I received from the deputy of the chief electoral officer to Hansard, and the figures will appear there. My impression was that only one province would have one less member.
